{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1548296-what-s-happens-when-a-court-refuses-to-give-up-power","id":1548296,"title":"What's happens when a court refuses to give up power?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-07T10:38:34-08:00","id":1548296,"title":"What's happens when a court refuses to give up power?","content":"Thinking of, potentially, starting a CtL game with some friends and the only idea I have for it is that the Summer Court has been in power for years, not just having influence, but refusing to give up the crown. Being the whole idea of the courts is shared power, what would happen to in this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T11:30:39-08:00","id":1548299,"title":"","content":"1e Core's signature city of Miami has as one of its standing complications the fact that the Summer Court has remained in power out of season for a long while, which historically resulted in the exile of the freehold's Spring Court and a more recent splinter group of the Court being allowed back in.<br /> <br /> Specifics are going to vary by freehold location and oaths, but at the very least while one court is holding power the freehold can't benefit from the Bargains of the other Courts. Possibly seasonal phenomena go slightly out of whack as well, particularly if the rituals that maintain the Bargains that empower the Courts are not allowed to be carried out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T13:55:27-08:00","id":1548306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1548296-what-s-happens-when-a-court-refuses-to-give-up-power?p=1548299#post1548299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e Core's signature city of Miami has as one of its standing complications the fact that the Summer Court has remained in power out of season for a long while, which historically resulted in the exile of the freehold's Spring Court and a more recent splinter group of the Court being allowed back in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the 1e book, how does this affect (effect?) True Fae, do they become more active in that area or anything like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T15:11:38-08:00","id":1548311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1548296-what-s-happens-when-a-court-refuses-to-give-up-power?p=1548306#post1548306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the 1e book, how does this affect (effect?) True Fae, do they become more active in that area or anything like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have any confirmed effect on the Fae within the city's writeup, 1e having no concrete Bargains baked into its systems, but the function of a Seasonal freehold cycling rulership still being to magically and/or logically baffle the Others means they're affected in the sense that at least some of the local Lost feel it's a bad omen and the Gentry aren't ones to turn down an open invitation. (I recall, but am presently having trouble finding, chapter fiction from 1e describing an army of Keepers gathering to descend on the City of Endless Summer.)<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that the Bargain does precisely nothing for anybody who does not belong to the Court and/or freehold it protects \u2014 the Gentry are still free to meddle with mortals with no greater strictures than normal exposure to Earthly atmosphere applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T21:29:18-08:00","id":1548318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1548296-what-s-happens-when-a-court-refuses-to-give-up-power?p=1548311#post1548311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have any confirmed effect on the Fae within the city's writeup, 1e having no concrete Bargains baked into its systems, but the function of a Seasonal freehold cycling rulership still being to magically and/or logically baffle the Others means they're affected in the sense that at least some of the local Lost feel it's a bad omen and the Gentry aren't ones to turn down an open invitation. (I recall, but am presently having trouble finding, chapter fiction from 1e describing an army of Keepers gathering to descend on the City of Endless Summer.)<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that the Bargain does precisely nothing for anybody who does not belong to the Court and/or freehold it protects \u2014 the Gentry are still free to meddle with mortals with no greater strictures than normal exposure to Earthly atmosphere applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening fiction for Lords of Summer, and the setting material for Miami does pretty well make it clear the True Fae are pressing in more often now that the Seasonal Pact is broken. Grandfather Thunder and the Summer Court are powerful enough to repel a lot of invaders, but the remaining courts of the Trident are eager to get to the root of Thunder's psyche/oaths and otherwise break their grip because the levee is starting to break from the pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-08T10:35:38-08:00","id":1548327,"title":"","content":"There's not much else I could add, but the Seasonal Courts were a means of defense against the True Far as they couldn't figure out how these Contracts would work as they would never think to share or cede power with anybody else.<br /> <br /> The Maimi thing must be a invitation to come on down as the power structure is something that they understand well.<br /> <br /> In addition with the breaking of the court structure would mean that the Lost might feel wary as the Seasonal Courts gave them something to feel safer as their world was turned upside down by their durance and having something like Seasonal Courts, Directional Courts or even the Sun and Moon Courts gave them something to latch on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-08-2025, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T07:44:18-08:00","id":1548517,"title":"","content":"In the <i>Motor City Breakdown</i> setting (link in my signature), all four of the seasonal courts refuse to share power, turning to the Detroit Metro area (and Windsor, ON) into an endless four-way turf war between opposed and competing gangs of hostile changelings. That might give you some ideas, if you need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}